digraph account_payable_process_76 {
	graph [rankdir=LR]
	START_NODE [label="" shape=circle width=0.3]
	subgraph CLUSTER_0 {
		"send to the vendor accounting department" [shape=box]
		"create a receiving report" [shape=box]
		"send to the vendor accounting department" -> "create a receiving report"
		"gather the receiving report" [shape=box]
		"create a receiving report" -> "gather the receiving report"
		"AND_SPLIT--4. Payment_NRB2" [label="+" fixedsize=true shape=diamond width=0.5]
		"gather the receiving report" -> "AND_SPLIT--4. Payment_NRB2"
		"enter the invoice into the accounts payable account" [shape=box]
		"AND_SPLIT--4. Payment_NRB2" -> "enter the invoice into the accounts payable account"
		"store in paid invoice file" [shape=box]
		"AND_SPLIT--4. Payment_NRB2" -> "store in paid invoice file"
		"AND_JOIN--4. Payment_NRB2" [label="+" fixedsize=true shape=diamond width=0.5]
		"enter the invoice into the accounts payable account" -> "AND_JOIN--4. Payment_NRB2"
		"store in paid invoice file" -> "AND_JOIN--4. Payment_NRB2"
	}
	START_NODE -> "send to the vendor accounting department"
	END_NODE [label="" shape=doublecircle width=0.2]
	"AND_JOIN--4. Payment_NRB2" -> END_NODE
	fontsize=15 label="\n\n
The following text is about the account payable process. It starts with sending to the vendor accounting department. 
When sending to the vendor accounting department is completed, you need to create a receiving report.
After creating a receiving report, gathering the receiving report needs to be done. 
Once gathering the receiving report occurs, the process is split into 2 parallel branches: entering the invoice into the accounts payable account and storing in paid invoice file. 
The process is now completed. 
"
}
